---
import BlogsLayout from '../../../layouts/blogslayout.astro';
---
<BlogsLayout title="PowerShell Script to Add Users in Intune Group" description="Automate enterprise group memberships in Microsoft Entra ID and Intune efficiently using advanced PowerShell scripting modules.">
  <header class="article-header">
    <h1>PowerShell Script to Add Users in Intune Group</h1>
    <p class="dek">Streamline endpoint compliance targeting by automating bulk user assignment into Microsoft Entra security groups using Microsoft Graph PowerShell SDK.</p>
    <p class="meta">By Akash Nagapure · August 2026 · 5 min read</p>
  </header>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Prerequisites & Graph API Connection</h2>
    <p>To manipulate group memberships securely, authenticate using the Microsoft.Graph module with appropriate permissions (`Group.ReadWrite.All`). Avoid legacy AzureAD modules as they are deprecated.</p>
    <h2>Sample Automation Script</h2>
    <p>Here is a clean snippet used to read a CSV list of user principal names (UPNs) and append them dynamically to your designated Intune targeted security group:</p>
    <pre style="background:#000; padding:1rem; border:1px solid rgba(56,189,248,0.2); border-radius:8px; overflow-x:auto;"><code style="color:#38bdf8; font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace; font-size:0.85rem;">
Connect-MgGraph -Scopes "Group.ReadWrite.All"
$GroupId = "your-target-group-object-id"
$Users = Import-Csv "C:\Temp\users.csv"

foreach ($User in $Users) {
    $UserObj = Get-MgUser -UserId $User.Email
    New-MgGroupMember -GroupId $GroupId -DirectoryObjectId $UserObj.Id
}
    </code></pre>
    <h2>Verification & Troubleshooting</h2>
    <p>Always inspect group logs or check the portal to verify membership synchronization speed, especially when handling dynamic versus assigned rules.</p>
  </div>
</BlogsLayout>
